Z||000000||Jncomutt||10-28-2001||06:48 PM||||Looking into buying an 85 GT.  The body is in decent shape as well as the interior.  Problem is a very bad engine knock.  Car will only do about 15 miles an hour.  I'm assuming that its the crank and the main/rod bearings.  Is this the right idea to go on and can it be repaired simply by changing the crank and the bearings to new ones???   I'd really like a V6/GT aero body style and hes only asking $500.   Any info would be appreciated.  TIA.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||10-28-2001||07:07 PM||||Might be something as simple as bearings, but I wouldn't count on it. Even the ones that I've heard about knocking could go faster than 15 MPH. Might be terminal. <BR>I'd count on replacing the long block. That way, if it's less serious, you won't be disappointed. <P>Just my $.02.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Some mornings, it just isn't worth chewing through the restraints.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||10-28-2001||07:21 PM||||oops<p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 10-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||10-28-2001||07:23 PM||||I think I'd buy it.<P>I do have a question though. What exactly does a "knock" sound like? What causes it? Ok so there were two questions.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">              <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Sootah||10-28-2001||07:38 PM||||I've become an expert on that particular sound in the short time that I've owned my 85 GT. The knock is rather immistakible (although you may go into denial about it as I did) It will knock faster at higher rpms but at different loads may be less severe or not present at all. (2nd and 3rd didn't knock all that bad, Neutral was worst)<P>I wasn't driving the car when it finally threw, Adam said it when whiiiir-thump then started running all quietly. Although with that quietness came a huge ass cloud of either steam or smoke out of the engine bay (I was behind him in his Civic, wanted him to listen to it)<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">     <BR><sup><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup>||||reg||4
Z||000005||maryjane||10-28-2001||08:38 PM||||so, what you're saying is "Adam blew up your engine!!" (Driver is ultimatly responsible) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Aknock can be several things. Piston pin-to-bushing slack, piston comes apart, valve drops down on piston, crankshaft broken.Too much clearance in rod bearings is most common culprit. The sound comes from the slack being taken up when the direction of travel changes from down to up-or vice versa. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jncomutt||10-28-2001||10:10 PM||||Thanx guys...  Either way, whatever the knock, I can buy it, have a great looking car in and out.   Just have another excuse to find that SC 3.8||||reg||1
